Design Notes/Decisions

a. Python will be used as the primary programming language.

b. Each sorting algorithm will be kept in its own .py file to keep the program organized.

c. The driver program will call the permutation generator and sorting algorithms.

d. Comparison counts will only include comparisons between array elements that determine their ordering.

e. The program will collect performance data for n = 4, 6, and 8.

f. The collected data will be used to determine the best 10 cases, worst 10 cases, and average number of comparisons for each sorting algorithm.
